# Citation metadata for this dataset. Format: https://citation-file-format.github.io/
# Each release pull request sets `version` and `date-released`. After Zenodo
# archives the release, its DOI goes under `identifiers` (and `doi`).
# See RELEASING.md.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, please cite it as below. If you rely on a specific
  word or rule, also cite the source and page given in that row.
type: dataset
title: "Papiamento: open data for Aruban Papiamento"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-20"
abstract: >-
  An open, citable reference dataset for Aruban Papiamento (pap-AW), written in
  the etymological orthography of the AB 2018 no. 68 law. It contains the
  headwords of the AB 2018 word list with English, Dutch and Spanish
  translations, numbers, calendar terms and public holidays, barbarismos,
  loanwords, closed word classes, proper names, verb forms, a Curaçao-to-Aruba
  spelling map, everyday sentence prompts for translation, and spelling and
  grammar rules in plain words and as machine-readable checker rules. Every row cites a source document and
  printed page, and carries a review status (draft, reviewed, disputed,
  deprecated).
authors:
  - name: "Papiamento Open Data contributors"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23427108"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23427108"
    description: "All versions (always resolves to the latest version)"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23427109"
    description: "Version 0.1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ARUBAGOV33/papiamento"
url: "https://github.com/ARUBAGOV33/papiamento"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - Papiamento
  - Aruba
  - Aruban Papiamento
  - pap-AW
  - creole language
  - orthography
  - spelling
  - lexicon
  - dictionary
  - grammar
  - language resources
  - natural language processing
  - machine translation
  - low-resource languages
  - open data
